      "content": "Skeptics often point to studies showing a correlation between DEI spending and *lower* stock performance, arguing that these programs are expensive distractions that don't translate to real profits.\nThey claim that many companies use DEI as a public relations tactic to look good to activists while ignoring actual systemic issues or even engaging in reverse discrimination.\nHowever, this view ignores the fact that the \"performative\" label usually applies only to companies that lack genuine commitment, whereas true DEI drives innovation and retention.\nYour board should recognize that while the critics have a point about *execution*, the consensus among top executives is that DEI is a necessary investment for long-term survival in a diverse market.",
